Why: gfortran >= 10 rejects calls of one external routine, in one file,
 that pass an array in one place and a scalar in another (or vice versa)
 for the same argument. Made consistent, without changing what is passed:
 - darrowheads.F, MUMPS_PROPINFO(LP, INFO, ...): the unit is ICNTL(1)
   (was the whole ICNTL array) and INFO is passed whole (was INFO(1) of
   a pointer);
 - dfac_lr.F, DGEMM: TEMP_BLOCK(1,1) instead of the whole allocatable
   TEMP_BLOCK, as for the other matrix arguments;
 - dsol_driver.F: IDUMMY(1), JDUMMY(1), KDUMMY(1) in the DMUMPS_SOL_C
   calls, C_Y(1) in two DMUMPS_GATHER_SOLUTION calls;
 - dfac_par_m.F, DMUMPS_MCAST2: DUMMY(1) instead of DUMMY.
Upstream: not sent; worth offering.
Obsolete when: upstream makes these calls consistent.

diff --git a/src/darrowheads.F b/src/darrowheads.F
index 4c93b3e..ef6290d 100644
--- a/src/darrowheads.F
+++ b/src/darrowheads.F
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ C
